{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nMorphisms whose image contains the generic points are dominant\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$Z \\subset S$", "MATH_0004": "$Z$", "MATH_0005": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-compact-dominant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:86b0fa53ed5784ef60226cc63d11cfd06bcc3b6388d6ee50e173b13166fd77e3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fa7e9e9650b5925eb16b0f2558814717b2203b3cb6afb5b7f8c1b988b18f79d7", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact morphism of schemes.\nThen <MATH_0002> is dominant if and only if for every irreducible\ncomponent <MATH_0003> the generic point of <MATH_0004> is in the\nimage of <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d86cbc2c9d5d97f38487fd677bc4ea53fd42327bd742babd46c499ec6dbd09ae", "unit_id": "tag:01RL:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$V \\subset S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$U_i \\subset f^{-1}(V)$", "MATH_0004": "$i = 1, \\ldots, n$", "MATH_0005": "$f^{-1}(V)$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nf' :\n\\coprod\\nolimits_{i = 1, \\ldots, n} U_i\n\\longrightarrow\nV.\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$V$", "MATH_0008": "$S$", "MATH_0009": "$V$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "MATH_0011": "$f'$", "MATH_0012": "$V, n, U_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-disjoint-union-affines}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-image-dense-generic-points}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:90f9d91d7097f1428ba6ca1750da2d5be992dd7aeba36c33b2f620e0160c1bce", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:671e2cc81b1384d51bb36adb88453509c4e9278f9d28449be0358a10804e6ffd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine open.\nBecause <MATH_0002> is quasi-compact we may choose finitely many affine\nopens <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004> covering\n<MATH_0005>. Consider the morphism of affines\n<MATH_0006>\nA disjoint union of affines is affine, see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nGeneric points of irreducible components of <MATH_0007>\nare exactly the generic points of the irreducible components of\n<MATH_0008> that meet <MATH_0009>. Also, <MATH_0010> is dominant if and only if <MATH_0011> is dominant\nno matter what choices of <MATH_0012> we make above. Thus we\nhave reduced the lemma to the case of a morphism of affine schemes.\nThe affine case is\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0c81e70a0f8ebea1be5c19f80a18f47950aeb02ccf43b143663dede8d93a6a31", "unit_id": "tag:01RL:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$g : S' \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f' : X' \\to S'$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$g$", "MATH_0006": "$g$", "MATH_0007": "$f'$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-dominant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:74c7c64821743d53b7988099ee60e755319ddcf4ec73bdf6a681a70123188bd9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7525b921bc7657ea1e7fff9176d6f7619d808402987c29014df4de682841e69c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact dominant morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism of schemes,  and let <MATH_0003>\nbe the base change of <MATH_0004> by <MATH_0005>. If generalizations lift along <MATH_0006>,\nthen <MATH_0007> is dominant.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aa0662b10607195e013af3d4d8b21e3efaa6e13e4d1193e9902054cc3366cff8", "unit_id": "tag:0H3F:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$g$", "MATH_0002": "$g$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-open-generizing}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-generalizations-lift-flat}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1890bf0f6a70138f84f0b5a8daa71ac65ff84055ce4675be9d10a836ddbdf994", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:da3bec5499c722b75f48c326bb93cb9f28e2c8c499d0b8499342f12752312228", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe will see that generalizations lift along <MATH_0001> if <MATH_0002> is open\n(Lemma <REF_0001>)\nor flat (Lemma <REF_0002>).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fa2da152dd5d3095fa46ed4bfccbdd763b057df08c7c61d0714fb8d7b4e92bda", "unit_id": "tag:01RI:prose-0004"}
